# Generated by cmd/bench: fresh per-attempt workspaces and sealed run
# results. Real production results live under /home/alex/data/results
# (docs/system-design.md section 3), outside this repository entirely;
# anything under build/ here is disposable local/dev scratch output.
/build/

# Vendor CLI binaries copied into the docker/ build context (see
# docker/README.md). These are ~215MB (claude) and ~258MB (codex) and are
# pinned per-operator, never committed.
/docker/claude
/docker/codex
/docker/codex-code-mode-host
tmp
.tmux.conf

# Evaluator-only data must never enter this repository. It lives outside it
# (the miner's gitignored output/), and these patterns exist so that a copy
# made here by mistake is caught by git rather than by a reviewer.
#
# The retrospective export is the more dangerous of the two: the correlated
# record is graded evidence, but patches/*.patch is the actual fix at line
# granularity. A patch committed here would be in published history and
# unrecoverable as a mistake.
*-evaluator-only/
correlated-report.json
patches/*.patch
